    </node>
    <node id="formula_0">
      <data key="d0">formula_0</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Formula_0 is the title or identifier of the given quadratic formula.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2a0888349718f5f2a20c6800cad13bbc-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781007343</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="a">
      <data key="d0">a</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">a is a coefficient in quadratic equations and formulas. It appears alongside another coefficient (often denoted as b) within the quadratic formula. In some contexts, it's multiplied by 2 and placed next to √ symbol. Additionally, a represents a numerical value used in various equations, including right triangles where it functions as one leg of a right triangle. Furthermore, a is recognized as a constant or variable representing an unknown value or measurement within the equation.

a also serves as a parameter of the integration operator. In another context, a represents another variable used in the formula, which is added to and subtracted from b. Additionally, a is one of the sides of a triangle in trigonometry. Furthermore, a is a variable in the mathematical expression. It can also be a base value or part of an index 1 value within the expression.

Moreover, a denotes a term in the sequence or series with subscripts indicating different terms. However, there are some inconsistencies and overlaps among these descriptions that need further clarification to avoid redundancy.&lt;SEP&gt;a is a variable used as the base in logarithmic expressions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2a0888349718f5f2a20c6800cad13bbc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-93b6acd960d94a31188c3d66a7ec9b38-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e104e211de2f2d77ed73269623c39fd2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-600a0c78af3d801d6496e749bbc4d6d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0d651681504c3b0d71951fb02e88df36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2b2765c1dc3c0924781f469247feb1d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-21f9ab7d714dddb9ee9e81d79d4dec8e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3686830df420ce5a2ede2561e500fcdd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-952ae85bc165a99a8207d50d0e4db44c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0c3cc366d264792a0e1c16b5d3be0262-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-23ec8458fb7fe841de5f228bb737b76f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f0395eac2737141afd769deb5c6140ea-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f205ae5d73886267042a8e0600bd6703-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2dfa7e1e54f19c7c0d453b57e49d569-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6cf4854854a42f4041e73060e773058f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b1e4448e5c567fada0f6d4ba573209ab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781008131</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="x">
      <data key="d0">x</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">x represents an unknown quantity or variable in various equations and expressions. It can be part of a quadratic equation where it denotes the solution, or simply any unknown value within an equation. Additionally, x is used as an independent variable in certain mathematical expressions and functions such as trigonometric functions like sine (sin) and cosine (cos). Furthermore, x also appears in the derivative of the cosine function, indicating its role in calculus contexts. It is the independent variable in the natural logarithm function. In limits, x serves as a parameter for the limit operator. The sine function uses x as an argument. x is used as the variable of integration. Additionally, x functions as the exponent in the exponential function and appears in various mathematical expressions.&lt;SEP&gt;x is a variable used in the mathematical expression.&lt;SEP&gt;x is a variable used in the formula.&lt;SEP&gt;x is a variable used in the mathematical expression.&lt;SEP&gt;x is a variable in the given formula.&lt;SEP&gt;x is a variable in the mathematical expression involving trigonometric functions.&lt;SEP&gt;x is the argument of the logarithm and natural logarithm functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2a0888349718f5f2a20c6800cad13bbc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e104e211de2f2d77ed73269623c39fd2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-600a0c78af3d801d6496e749bbc4d6d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0d651681504c3b0d71951fb02e88df36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4241bc197dcc704273a7b7e735b97ac-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e199e2c6f7381d60c9ac07baabe0b381-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d0dd84a0be328b9a9b4a65c28c5d2ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b43fc5cd8aa611e5651d7cf5010dcc6b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-03a5738df2fb27efe596a610bf0b8dfe-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b176d9daac368c608373bc3d18f28da-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-952ae85bc165a99a8207d50d0e4db44c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-93205e0c8c751a55081db85cf6bc6a62-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-946f7f65b47d02934ef52ad10ee466e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0522860145c2ef82958731f8d13ec3e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b5a606db4a1d6eb64b1b4f497a8a132-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a0dbd6564ebc2644ef1cc840ebfe51a2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a83710e679a36bae4dc9d13ef1fef596-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-77e6c803852efe2c5d828dcee4d05d91-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b1de46266243c31cf0c96ded454f6a13-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-93a94f006c522d695912e86f3a1ab972-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b1e4448e5c567fada0f6d4ba573209ab-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781008131</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="b">
      <data key="d0">b</data>
      <data key="d1">variable</data>
      <data key="d2">Entity b is a numerical value used in quadratic equations and formulas. It appears twice within the quadratic formula, specifically subtracted from the square root of D. Additionally, in certain contexts, such as right triangles or integral expressions, b can represent another variable involved in subtraction with c.&lt;SEP&gt;b represents another side of a triangle in trigonometry.&lt;SEP&gt;b is another variable in the mathematical expression.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2a0888349718f5f2a20c6800cad13bbc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-93b6acd960d94a31188c3d66a7ec9b38-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e104e211de2f2d77ed73269623c39fd2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-600a0c78af3d801d6496e749bbc4d6d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2b2765c1dc3c0924781f469247feb1d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-21f9ab7d714dddb9ee9e81d79d4dec8e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-952ae85bc165a99a8207d50d0e4db44c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0c3cc366d264792a0e1c16b5d3be0262-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-23ec8458fb7fe841de5f228bb737b76f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f0395eac2737141afd769deb5c6140ea-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781008078</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="c">
      <data key="d0">c</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">c is a constant term in the quadratic equation.&lt;SEP&gt;c is yet another coefficient in a quadratic equation, present in the formula as well.&lt;SEP&gt;The number c is a constant in the equation.&lt;SEP&gt;The third variable in the equation, also representing a numerical value.&lt;SEP&gt;c represents the hypotenuse in the context of the Pythagorean theorem.&lt;SEP&gt;c represents one of the variables used in the formula, which are squared and compared to other terms.&lt;SEP&gt;c represents yet another side of a triangle in trigonometry.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2a0888349718f5f2a20c6800cad13bbc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-93b6acd960d94a31188c3d66a7ec9b38-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0d651681504c3b0d71951fb02e88df36-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2b2765c1dc3c0924781f469247feb1d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-21f9ab7d714dddb9ee9e81d79d4dec8e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0c3cc366d264792a0e1c16b5d3be0262-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-23ec8458fb7fe841de5f228bb737b76f-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781008062</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="x^2">
      <data key="d0">x^2</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2a0888349718f5f2a20c6800cad13bbc-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">a is added to x^2.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781007343</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="D">
      <data key="d0">D</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">D represents the discriminant in a quadratic equation.&lt;SEP&gt;D is under the square root symbol and represents the discriminant in a quadratic equation.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-93b6acd960d94a31188c3d66a7ec9b38-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e104e211de2f2d77ed73269623c39fd2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781007362</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="b^2">
      <data key="d0">b^2</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-93b6acd960d94a31188c3d66a7ec9b38-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0c3cc366d264792a0e1c16b5d3be0262-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">b is raised to the power of 2 before being subtracted from D.&lt;SEP&gt;The b squared term is subtracted from D in the given formula.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781007354</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="4a">
      <data key="d0">4a</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-93b6acd960d94a31188c3d66a7ec9b38-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">4 times a is added to the result of b squared before being subtracted from D to form the discriminant.&lt;SEP&gt;4 times a is subtracted from b squared to form D.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1781007354</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
