    <node id="e">
      <data key="d0">e</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The constant e represents Euler's number, which is approximately equal to 2.71828 and is crucial in calculus and analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Euler's number, a fundamental constant in mathematics and calculus.&lt;SEP&gt;e is a mathematical constant representing the base of natural logarithm.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-4bb262ebbff0da390377af441dcb84fa-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-93205e0c8c751a55081db85cf6bc6a62-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c5ba0dcacc2438267b920d857cb7d2c1-chunk-000</data>
