    <node id="C">
      <data key="d0">C</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The constant of integration, a term added to indefinite integrals.&lt;SEP&gt;C represents the constant of integration in the formula.&lt;SEP&gt;C represents an integration constant.&lt;SEP&gt;C denotes an angle within the formula, where cosine (cos) of C is applied to the calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;C denotes an angle in a triangle, with C being the reference angle in this context.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-93205e0c8c751a55081db85cf6bc6a62-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-946f7f65b47d02934ef52ad10ee466e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0522860145c2ef82958731f8d13ec3e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0c3cc366d264792a0e1c16b5d3be0262-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-23ec8458fb7fe841de5f228bb737b76f-chunk-000</data>
